.TH MAIL-CONFIG-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mail-config-audit \- read-only static review of Postfix configuration text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mail-config-audit
.RB [ --main " ABSOLUTE_PATH]
.RB [ --master " ABSOLUTE_PATH]
.RB [ --null ]
.br
.B mail-config-audit
.BR --help " | " --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads explicit settings in
.I main.cf
and optionally identifies unverified service overrides in
.IR master.cf .
Does not execute Postfix, access the network, follow inclusion directives,
modify files, evaluate lookup maps, expand Postfix parameters, check TLS
certificates or establish the live server configuration.
.PP
The standard report contains LEVEL, SOURCE, LINE and CODE followed by issue
and note counts. Values, secrets and raw configuration text are not printed.
A report without static issues is not proof of a safe mail relay or secure
SMTP authentication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --main " PATH"
Absolute path of main.cf (default: /etc/postfix/main.cf).
.TP
.BI --master " PATH"
Optional absolute path of master.cf. Recognized service -o overrides yield
review notes rather than false assumptions about effective values.
.TP
.B --null
Use NUL-terminated four-field records for findings and summary.
.TP
.BR --help , " -h"
Display help.
.TP
.B --version
Display tool version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No definite static issues detected (not a security certification).
.TP
.B 1
One or more static issues detected.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Unavailable, unreadable, oversized or malformed inputs or runtime error.
.SH LIMITATIONS
At most 2 MiB and 10,000 lines per file, 16 KiB per physical line.
No evaluation of Postfix defaults, environment, service overrides, expansion,
access maps, active listeners or effective relay policy.
Master.cf uses only a partial parser and all detected overrides require
manual inspection. No partial report on an input failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR postconf (1),
.BR postconf (5),
.BR master (5)
